---
// Kruskal on 5 stocks, distances chosen by hand (not market data). Python (networkx) check:
// MST edges (0,1)=0.6 (1,2)=1.05 (2,3)=0.7 (3,4)=0.5, total 2.85; edge (2,4)=0.8 closes a cycle and is skipped.
const W = 900, H = 360;
const P: [number, number][] = [[80, 120], [210, 70], [340, 150], [470, 90], [590, 190]];
const names = ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E'];
const steps = [
  { a: 4, b: 3, d: 0.5, ok: true, n: 1, lx: 16, ly: -2, an: 'start' },
  { a: 0, b: 1, d: 0.6, ok: true, n: 2 },
  { a: 2, b: 3, d: 0.7, ok: true, n: 3 },
  { a: 2, b: 4, d: 0.8, ok: false, n: 4 },
  { a: 1, b: 2, d: 1.05, ok: true, n: 5 },
];
// tree drawn on a sub-canvas (x 20..620), steps list on the right
---
<figure class="atp11-kr">
  <div class="atp11-kr-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Kruskal's algorithm on five stocks A to E. Edges are taken in order of distance: D-E 0.5, A-B 0.6, C-D 0.7 are kept; C-E 0.8 would close a cycle C-D-E so it is skipped; B-C 1.05 joins the last two groups. Four edges, total length 2.85.">
      <text x="20" y="26" class="h"><tspan data-lang-en>Building the tree: take the shortest link that adds a new stock</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Dựng cây: lấy cạnh ngắn nhất còn nối thêm được một mã mới</tspan></text>
      {steps.map((s) => (
        <line x1={P[s.a][0]} y1={P[s.a][1]} x2={P[s.b][0]} y2={P[s.b][1]} class={s.ok ? 'e-ok' : 'e-skip'} />
      ))}
      {steps.map((s) => {
        const mx = (P[s.a][0] + P[s.b][0]) / 2, my = (P[s.a][1] + P[s.b][1]) / 2;
        return <text x={mx + (s.lx ?? 0)} y={my + (s.ly ?? -8)} text-anchor={s.an ?? 'middle'} class={s.ok ? 'el' : 'el skip'}>{s.d.toFixed(2)}</text>;
      })}
      {P.map(([x, y], i) => (
        <g>
          <circle cx={x} cy={y} r="17" class="node" />
          <text x={x} y={y + 5} text-anchor="middle" class="nl">{names[i]}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <text x="20" y="300" class="sub"><tspan data-lang-en>Distances are made up for the drawing. Gold = kept, dashed red = skipped.</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Khoảng cách là số dựng cho hình. Vàng = giữ, đỏ nét đứt = bỏ qua.</tspan></text>
      <text x="20" y="324" class="sub"><tspan data-lang-en>5 stocks need 4 edges; total length 0.5 + 0.6 + 0.7 + 1.05 = 2.85.</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>5 mã cần 4 cạnh; tổng độ dài 0,5 + 0,6 + 0,7 + 1,05 = 2,85.</tspan></text>
      <text x="670" y="66" class="sh"><tspan data-lang-en>Edges, shortest first</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Các cạnh, ngắn nhất trước</tspan></text>
      {steps.map((s, i) => (
        <g>
          <rect x="670" y={80 + i * 46} width="210" height="36" rx="6" class={s.ok ? 'row ok' : 'row skip'} />
          <text x="684" y={103 + i * 46} class="rl">{names[s.a]}–{names[s.b]}  {s.d.toFixed(2)}</text>
          <text x="868" y={103 + i * 46} text-anchor="end" class={s.ok ? 'rv ok' : 'rv skip'}>
            {s.ok ? <><tspan data-lang-en>keep</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>giữ</tspan></> : <><tspan data-lang-en>cycle, skip</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>thành vòng, bỏ</tspan></>}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))}
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Kruskal's algorithm: sort every pair by distance, then keep a link only if it joins two stocks that are not yet connected. The result has N−1 links and no loops.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Thuật toán Kruskal: sắp mọi cặp theo khoảng cách, rồi chỉ giữ cạnh nào nối hai mã chưa liên thông. Kết quả có N−1 cạnh và không có vòng.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .atp11-kr { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .atp11-kr-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .atp11-kr svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .atp11-kr text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .atp11-kr .h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .atp11-kr .sh { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .atp11-kr .sub { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .atp11-kr .nl { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .atp11-kr .el { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--text); }
  .atp11-kr .el.skip { fill: var(--red); }
  .atp11-kr .rl { font-size: 13.5px; fill: var(--text); }
  .atp11-kr .rv { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; }
  .atp11-kr .rv.ok { fill: var(--text); }
  .atp11-kr .rv.skip { fill: var(--red); }
  .atp11-kr .e-ok { stroke: var(--gold-icon); stroke-width: 3; }
  .atp11-kr .e-skip { stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 2; stroke-dasharray: 5 5; }
  .atp11-kr .node { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .atp11-kr .row { stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .atp11-kr .row.ok { fill: var(--gold-tint-bg); stroke: var(--gold-icon); }
  .atp11-kr .row.skip { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); }
  .atp11-kr figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
